Mutual Fund → A Mutual fund is a pool of money collected from various investors and invest in capital market instruments such as shares, Bonds & govt. securities. It is managed by professional fund managers. The income earned through these investment is shared by its unit holders in proportion to the number of units owned by them. AMC
It is the price at which unit of MF are bought & sold
NAV → It is a fund’s market value per unit. It is calculated on daily basis.
NAV = Value of Cash & Securities in fund portfolio - liabilities
